{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138387-w5-thoughts","id":1138387,"title":"W5 thoughts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-07T13:51:13-07:00","id":1138387,"title":"W5 thoughts","content":"So after looking over the new V5 book, it made me wonder. When they get to Werewolf will they take the same hunger system and convert it over to rage? Will werewolf have to worry that any roll could send them over the edge at any moment. All I can see is a frustrated Glasswalker at the DMV waiting in line talking to someone in line and flipping out because of a bad roll. I am wondering what other people thoughts on this since it seems they are very hung up on the hunger system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T18:04:47-07:00","id":1138467,"title":"","content":"That sounds BAD, to me.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T00:09:55-07:00","id":1138523,"title":"","content":"While I think that the Rage and Frenzy mechanics in WtA are in a significant need of an overhaul, the V5 previews are not at all how that should go.<br /> <br /> That said, I do wholly expect that WW will do exactly this with W5 unless V5 tanks irrevocably badly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T01:34:06-07:00","id":1138529,"title":"","content":"Randomizing thirst i V5 is a bit bad for me and Yes, doing the same in W5 is very wrong. I don't have any idea how rebuild frenzy and rage cause I'm accustomed to present stuff. Tearing the rage points from werewolf is anathema to my mind, cause spending them for more actions is in my opinion adventage over regular npc in combat and that my player loves most. Doing that means that most of gifts need rebuilding, The same thing is gnosis. Cutting the pool from max 10 to max 5 for example means that you can use less gifts based on rage/gnosis in scene. The worst thing is that using gnosis and rage in one turn is impossible. It sounds very munchkin but it is just a part of system mechanics. Cutting blood/rage pool in Vampire and Werewolf against regular human means that we have only half of possibilities in combat. My players carefully counts every point in every confrontation cause more actions/gifts are more adventages (shapeshifiting and form bonuses are the other part of stuff). With cutting the pool , rebuilding the gifts is necessary. Or! they will create something new. The best part is ... I can always use W20 or older werewolf. No one is staying above my head with an axe ready to fall if I won't but new WW rpg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T01:50:00-07:00","id":1138533,"title":"","content":"While I don't want to derail this into a house rules for Rage thread, the issue with the current rules is that in an effort to have elegance in how Frenzies work (roll Rage for all potential ways to Frenzy) the game makes other things really messy. The relatively simple fix is to have two distinct mechanical paths to Frenzy. First is purposefully channeling Rage (aka rolling Rage as a dice-pool in the various subsystems where you do that) that carries a risk of going overboard and Frenzy (which is already how it works, though individual implementations could use some tweaking and there's no reason to hold everything to the 4/6 success thresholds, also low Rage characters don't Frenzy this way but they get shit dice-pools for using this option). Second is resisting stimuli, which should be something more like rolling Willpower at a difficulty modified by your Rage. This second bit is important because it makes Frenzy relevant to low Rage characters without racking up huge temporary Rage tallies. Rolling to resist is also much easier on the WoD base system than rolling to fail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T13:01:06-07:00","id":1138681,"title":"","content":"Id like to see the gift Infallbe Argument of logic fixed, possibly divided into 3 or 4 gifs<br /> <br /> the designers were right about one thing; the garou DID need a upgrade in Mind fuck magic.<br /> <br /> but ffect should either decayith time, or have a gnosis cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T13:12:59-07:00","id":1138686,"title":"","content":"Looking at the amount of Requiem that is currently in the Alpha of V5,,,,,maybe there will be a whole bunch of Forsaken in W5? Honestly my thoughts on W5 range between 'get these numptys away from my favourite game' and ' I wonder if I'll even recognise it.'<br /> <br /> Luckily I have all my 1st through to W20 books and I'll just keep using those when ( based on current trends in WW games) W5 proves to be utter pants. Though with the Storytellers Vault up at least we should be getting more W20 books even if they're not from Onyx Path anymore.....I mean, sure, a lot will be B.J. Zanzibaresque but I have faith there are some top notch undiscovered writers out there that will surprise me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T19:42:17-07:00","id":1138783,"title":"","content":"What I suspect is that you will have various things you can do that call upon rage or give you rage dice. Rage dice lead to Frenzy. WIth composure being used to control situations better. I expect this leads to alot of &quot;my werewolf watches fox News in the woods so he can reset his frenzies when alone!&quot;<br /> <br /> I expect we will see a similar mechanic for Paradox, Angst, Banality...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T09:27:30-07:00","id":1139717,"title":"","content":"I haven't looked at the V5 pdf itself, but my tabletop group went to a discussion panel at Dragoncon where the game developers talked about the way V5 is going to treat blood pools and hunger and frenzy. We all liked the concept for vampires; however, I'm don't think an analogous treatment of garou rage would work, because there's no werewolf equivalent to vampiric hunger that would continually be driven higher by using rage. In other words, nothing like hunger for more blood increases when you spend rage. It would seem self-contradictory for loss of rage to cause frenzy, because it's the garou rage itself that makes self-control difficult for them.<br /> <br /> Also the stated motive for changing the use of blood pools (as we heard in the Dragoncon panel) is to keep the players from the risk of completely losing their blood-fueled powers while giving them motives to do things in the game keep themselves balanced. A better analogy, in my opinion, if the developers want to make a similar change in Werewolf, would be uncapping the use of gnosis, and letting that drive the risk of frenzy. In &quot;cinematic&quot; terms, loss of gnosis would cause a stressful craving that weakens your self-control until you do something about your low gnosis.<br /> <br /> But really we're speculating on how a good idea for V5 might be shoe-horned into W5, and I'm not convinced the designers think they'll have to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T13:10:20-07:00","id":1139753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138387-w5-thoughts?p=1138681#post1138681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Id like to see the gift Infallbe Argument of logic fixed, possibly divided into 3 or 4 gifs<br /> <br /> the designers were right about one thing; the garou DID need a upgrade in Mind fuck magic.<br /> <br /> but ffect should either decayith time, or have a gnosis cost.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are many gifts that need fixing, but Shadow Lords do have the most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T13:24:06-07:00","id":1139755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138387-w5-thoughts?p=1139717#post1139717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't looked at the V5 pdf itself, but my tabletop group went to a discussion panel at Dragoncon where the game developers talked about the way V5 is going to treat blood pools and hunger and frenzy. We all liked the concept for vampires; however, I'm don't think an analogous treatment of garou rage would work, because there's no werewolf equivalent to vampiric hunger that would continually be driven higher by using rage. In other words, nothing like hunger for more blood increases when you spend rage. It would seem self-contradictory for loss of rage to cause frenzy, because it's the garou rage itself that makes self-control difficult for them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They have been pushing the Garou vs Humans angle pretty hard, so there is a chance that munching on the long pig will become much more common.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T22:18:32-07:00","id":1139832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138387-w5-thoughts?p=1139717#post1139717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't looked at the V5 pdf itself, but my tabletop group went to a discussion panel at Dragoncon where the game developers talked about the way V5 is going to treat blood pools and hunger and frenzy. We all liked the concept for vampires; however, I'm don't think an analogous treatment of garou rage would work, because there's no werewolf equivalent to vampiric hunger that would continually be driven higher by using rage. In other words, nothing like hunger for more blood increases when you spend rage. It would seem self-contradictory for loss of rage to cause frenzy, because it's the garou rage itself that makes self-control difficult for them.<br /> <br /> Also the stated motive for changing the use of blood pools (as we heard in the Dragoncon panel) is to keep the players from the risk of completely losing their blood-fueled powers while giving them motives to do things in the game keep themselves balanced. A better analogy, in my opinion, if the developers want to make a similar change in Werewolf, would be uncapping the use of gnosis, and letting that drive the risk of frenzy. In &quot;cinematic&quot; terms, loss of gnosis would cause a stressful craving that weakens your self-control until you do something about your low gnosis.<br /> <br /> But really we're speculating on how a good idea for V5 might be shoe-horned into W5, and I'm not convinced the designers think they'll have to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think people are thinking Rage will function as something you spend in w5, but rather I imagine if they are using the same chasis Rage naturally builds up and you want to be constantly burnning it off unless you want to frenzy, but there aren't alot of &quot;Safe&quot; ways to burn it off. So you get Rage compulsions and Frenzy with Composure being worked in as a similar mitigation mechanic as for Vampires.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T18:03:59-07:00","id":1140373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138387-w5-thoughts?p=1139755#post1139755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They have been pushing the Garou vs Humans angle pretty hard, so there is a chance that munching on the long pig will become much more common.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1Q8gZ8mQufU\" data-code=\"1Q8gZ8mQufU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/1Q8gZ8mQufU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T14:53:13-07:00","id":1140652,"title":"","content":"I agree with Saur Ops, you can't put the genie back in the bottle with humanity. It's so large and powerful a force that actually trying to start the Impergium back up will just mean the Garou will be hunted to extinction very quickly. Besides, while they enact the Wyrm and Weaver's will they are in part a symptom of the spiritual imbalance, not always the cause. I think nuWW trying to emphasize this angle is another example of them trying to be edgy and cool in a rather ham fisted manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T16:09:58-07:00","id":1140668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138387-w5-thoughts?p=1140652#post1140652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with Saur Ops, you can't put the genie back in the bottle with humanity. It's so large and powerful a force that actually trying to start the Impergium back up will just mean the Garou will be hunted to extinction very quickly. Besides, while they enact the Wyrm and Weaver's will they are in part a symptom of the spiritual imbalance, not always the cause. I think nuWW trying to emphasize this angle is another example of them trying to be edgy and cool in a rather ham fisted manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do somewhat understand the want for it. A common complaint with WtA from general werewolf fiction fans has been that they don't really resemble werewolves. There is no horror of becoming a monster, the focus isn't on dealing with the Change but instead on saving the enviroment. Given how many times -that- has been kryptonite to people, focus change was needed. Now it would be monstrous werewolves attacking and eating(?) humans, maybe even having their condition transferred through a bite. Making them more like -actual- werewolves.<br /> <br /> Mind, I don't think this is smart. Garou aren't really werewolves as much as a fantasy race, but it works and has worked for a while. Besides, dumping down the complex issue of Wyrm's influence to just Humanity being the issue is lazy to me. Best moment of werewolf have been moments where garou have had to face an issue they can't shred to pieces, but have to find a spiritual solution and shred the issue with THAT.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T17:46:34-07:00","id":1140683,"title":"","content":"Considering how early they are into the development of the rules for Vampire and that whole, Werewolf is a separate game that is likely to have a separate developer thing. Not QUITE ready to jump on the panic for no reason based on an alpha of another game line's train just yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 09-15-2017, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T18:11:48-07:00","id":1140687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138387-w5-thoughts?p=1140668#post1140668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do somewhat understand the want for it. A common complaint with WtA from general werewolf fiction fans has been that they don't really resemble werewolves. There is no horror of becoming a monster, the focus isn't on dealing with the Change but instead on saving the enviroment. Given how many times -that- has been kryptonite to <b>SOME</b> people, focus change was needed. Now it would be monstrous werewolves attacking and eating(?) humans, maybe even having their condition transferred through a bite. Making them more like -actual- werewolves.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I'd say with the massive success of the W20 Kickstarters no focus change was needed at all, and, like with V5, it would just be change for the sake of change.<br /> <br /> That said a game about modern Victorian-folkloric werewolves would be playing as a normal person for 27-30 nights a month then handing your Character sheet <br /> to the GM for 1-4 nights and so on. It would also need to include rubbing on linament to change into a werewolf, chances of turning into a vampire when fatally wounded, Also transformation through having had your mother crawl through horse placenta while giving birth, or if the midwife passed you through a birch hoop....or drinking water from a wolfs pawprint.....or eat from a wolfs kill....or...etc.<br /> <br /> In regards to games about hunting humans ( and spirits, and claimed etc) and bite transferred conditions; theres already a game for that, its called Forsaken.<br /> <br /> The garou for the most part go unnoticed by humans; its the occasions where they fuck up they gave rise to the human legends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 09-15-2017, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T20:40:55-07:00","id":1140712,"title":"","content":"There's plenty of revulsion and shock in being a Garou, and they are werewolves more than a fantasy race. It's just that a lot of said revulsion involves the revelation of what humans have been doing to the place, writ as plain as day in the Umbra and magnified by Rage, and in the deeds of the Garou's ancestors, what with the Impergium and Wars of Rage and all. Their new society says that their ancestors were great heroes, and maybe a lot of them are, but then you have the Garou's answers to Columbus and Forrest... and their spirits are a part of your lineage. They can and will talk to you, even if you'd really wish they wouldn't. If you have a certain flaw, they'll even possess you.<br /> <br /> (On another front, Garou who were raised to have very chauvinistic attitudes about human self-awareness and other touted &quot;unique&quot; qualities are going to be in for a, shall we say, spiritually-taxing time when this notion breaks down in grand style and the cosmos smears the dust in their faces.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138387-w5-thoughts?p=1140687#post1140687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The garou for the most part go unnoticed by humans; its the occasions where they fuck up they gave rise to the human legends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like that punishment rite that causes a human who has wronged one of the people to assume Crinos during the full moon and go on a killing spree. You could replace the Impergium with that rite being abused and it would probably serve the same narrative end.<br /> <br /> (Reference: Curse of the Wolf, Werewolf: the Dark Ages p114)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T01:56:24-07:00","id":1140742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1138387-w5-thoughts?p=1140687#post1140687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly I'd say with the massive success of the W20 Kickstarters no focus change was needed at all, and, like with V5, it would just be change for the sake of change.<br /> <br /> That said a game about modern Victorian-folkloric werewolves would be playing as a normal person for 27-30 nights a month then handing your Character sheet<br /> to the GM for 1-4 nights and so on. It would also need to include rubbing on linament to change into a werewolf, chances of turning into a vampire when fatally wounded, Also transformation through having had your mother crawl through horse placenta while giving birth, or if the midwife passed you through a birch hoop....or drinking water from a wolfs pawprint.....or eat from a wolfs kill....or...etc.<br /> <br /> In regards to games about hunting humans ( and spirits, and claimed etc) and bite transferred conditions; theres already a game for that, its called Forsaken.<br /> <br /> The garou for the most part go unnoticed by humans; its the occasions where they fuck up they gave rise to the human legends.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the image would be more that werewolves should not be bound by one morality and they should infect people and eat them freely, depending on their personal morality.<br /> <br /> Forsaken is indeed the better game for that, of course.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}